t status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TERADA, JUNJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAHA HATSUDOKI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TERADA JUNJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TERADA, JUNJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An electric vehicle power supply system (402) in which the actual capacity, i.e., the maximum capacity learned value at the present time, of a chargeable battery (400) when the battery (400) is used cyclically is found, comprising discharging means (403) for performing a refresh discharging of the battery (400), discharging control means (404) for controlling the discharging means (403) so that the refresh discharging is performed with a discharging current the waveform of which includes a pulse waveform, and actual capacity learning means (405) for finding the actual capacity of the battery (400) from the discharge capacity including the discharging capacity during the refresh discharging.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Système (402) d'alimentation électrique pour un véhicule, qui permet de trouver la capacité effective, c'est-à-dire la valeur déterminée de capacité maximale dans l'instant, d'une batterie rechargeable (400) lorsque ladite batterie est utilisée de manière cyclique. Ledit système comporte un moyen de décharge (403) destiné à effectuer une décharge de régénération de la batterie (400), un moyen de commande (404) de décharge destiné à commander le moyen de décharge (403) de manière que la décharge de régénération soit effectuée avec un courant de décharge dont la forme d'onde comporte un signal impulsionnel, et un moyen de détermination (405) de la capacité effective destiné à trouver la capacité effective de la batterie (400) sur la base de la capacité de décharge, y compris la capacité de décharge pendant la décharge de régénération.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>